<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Alawite State</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1936 CE · capital Latakia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A French-created state for the Alawite mountains and coast of Syria, separated from the rest of Syria between 1920 and 1936.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1920 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> established the Territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alawites">Alawites</a>, covering the coastal mountains and the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latakia">Latakia</a>, where the Alawites, a heterodox Shia community long marginalised under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, were the majority in the countryside. The territory became the Alawite State in 1922.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governed by French officials with an Alawite-dominated representative council, the state withdrew from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-federation">Syrian Federation</a> in 1924 and was renamed the Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latakia">Latakia</a> in 1930. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recruited many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alawites">Alawites</a> into its colonial army. Road-building and land reform were undertaken, but the coastal towns, largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> and Christian, favoured union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the 1936 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-treaty-of-independence">Franco-Syrian treaty</a> the state was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-republic">Syrian Republic</a>, despite petitions by some Alawite notables asking to remain separate, and it was fully integrated in 1937.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/alawite-state.jpg" alt="Alawite State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: AnonMoos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Alawite_State_(1920%E2%80%931936).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1936 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Latakia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ernest Schoeffler</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Alawite Islam, Sunni Islam, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>State of Alawites, State of Latakia, Territory of the Alawites</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=alawite-state" aria-label="Alawite State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5584 894 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Alawite State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5904 1150L5905 1205M5904 1150L5927 1218"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5905 1205h0M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5904 1150h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5904 1150h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Latakia. <a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=alawite-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
